# LRSWEEP frozen analysis rule — 2026-09-10

`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM`. This file was written before any sweep fit ran.

- Routes and learning rates: C1, C2, C3 crossed with
  `{1e-4, 3e-4, 1e-3, 3e-3, 1e-2, 3e-2, 1e-1}`.
- Architecture, activation, Adam betas/epsilon, weight decay, route loss and
  gauge weights are the literals in `src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py`. Only
  `learning_rate` is passed as an overridden literal to `AdamMLPHead.create`.
- One first sealed pilot learner seed is used, as in the primary C1REAL and
  C2REAL leave-one-anchor-out (LOAO) measurements.
- Checkpoints: initial state (diagnostic only) and epochs 100, 200, 300, 400,
  500. Reported checkpoints are 100–500.
- Objective stabilization tolerance: absolute 400→500 change no greater than
  1% of `max(abs(objective_at_400), 1e-12)`.
- Held-out stabilization tolerances: absolute 400→500 changes no greater than
  0.01 for level R², 0.005 for within-group ordering, and 0.005 for top-1.
- A cell is admissible on convergence grounds exactly when it is finite through
  epoch 500 and all four stabilization checks pass. Quality does not select or
  break ties among admissible rates.
- “Last material improvement” is the destination epoch of the last adjacent
  checkpoint interval, including 0→100, whose objective decrease exceeds its
  relative tolerance or whose predictive-metric increase exceeds that metric's
  absolute tolerance. `none` means no such sampled interval.
- Divergence means a non-finite objective or parameter. The earliest update
  epoch is recorded.
- Parameter L2 norm includes trainable weights and biases, excludes Adam
  moments, and is summarized across LOAO fold models.
- C1 input: the same 37-anchor coherent prefix of the repaired Q1 v2 exact-row
  panel used by C1REALV2.
- C2 input: the same 20-anchor exact-row panel used by C2REAL. Q1 v2 has no Q2
  schema and its public projection copies `q2_state` byte-for-byte, so this is
  explicitly Q2 schema v1.
- C3 input: the twelve completed two-world anchors (steps 0–5) present before
  this file was written in the live C3REAL exact-row directory, restricted by
  filename rather than a later-changing glob; C3 uses its available v2 route
  state. The live directory is read only.
- Predictive metrics use the C1REAL definitions. For C3, one anchor is one
  candidate group and the declared hard zeros for empty/singleton coalitions
  are retained in evaluation while only size>=2 rows train the head.
- Loss is a convergence diagnostic only and is never evidence about EE. No EE
  quantity, production training, policy run, or acceptance test is computed.
