100: 24}`. Hence 78.63% of evaluation rows are singletons and 21.27% are
trainable nontrivial coalitions. Direct inspection of all twelve frozen NPZ
inputs found exact zero Psi on all 9,394 singleton rows. The one completed
per-process generator receipt available at validation time (world 1, step 0)
reported maximum decomposition residual `8.882e-15`; the remaining live
generator ranges had not yet emitted their process-level receipts, so no
all-anchor decomposition claim is made here.

[DERIVED] C3 singleton targets must be zero because
`Psi_{i} = Delta F({i}) - d_i`, while `d_i` is that same unilateral increment.
The full-support C3 R² values are therefore strongly aided by structurally easy
zeros; they should not be read as evidence of a well-fitted interaction head.

All LOAO fits used the first sealed pilot seed
`V025_LEARNER/seed/1` (`6407676579069309528`), the literal sealed architectures
and optimizer fields, and one deterministic full-batch Adam update per epoch.
Only the learning-rate field passed to `AdamMLPHead.create` changed. C1/C2 used
the same deterministic 4,096-pair cap as C1REAL/C2REAL. C3 aggregated all
training-anchor gradients into one full-batch update per epoch and hard-set
empty/singleton predictions to zero.

[RUN] The common-initialization parameter L2 norms were `4.4561` (C1),
`19.9039` (C2), and `16.0125` (C3). The epoch-500 tables give fold means and
