## What is verified, derived, and inferred

[RUN] The machine result contains seven points per route, all five requested
checkpoints per point, all 21 epoch-500 parameter-norm summaries, the constant
floors, and the earliest-divergence field. All input hashes matched before and
after. `learner.py` remained byte-identical at SHA-256
`09fc781b273f42fce3913c57150187a18f05b100155027c53e023abae3f46a01`.

[RUN] The sweep used only
`/home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python`, one Python process,
`nice=15`, and all BLAS thread variables equal to one. Its printed peak line
was `PEAK_RSS_KB=113016` (about 110.4 MiB), far below 5 GiB. It did not write
to the C2 or C3 source workspaces or any live-job directory.

[DERIVED] A decreasing training objective with degrading held-out R² is not a
contradiction: they are evaluated on different anchor partitions. It is also
not an EE statement. Parameter L2 is reported over weights and biases only;
the mean and range are over LOAO fold models, not over learner seeds.

[INFERRED] The parameter-scale gradients and continuing loss motion distinguish
these cases from collapsed constant heads. But because no rate satisfies the
fixed convergence condition, predictive-quality differences among rates must
not be used to choose a winner from this run. A longer prospectively declared
horizon (or a separate optimization-validity design) is required before any
learning rate can be certified for these architectures.

